    "text": "def same_chars(s0: str, s1: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if two words have the same characters.\n    >>> same_chars('eabcdzzzz', 'dddzzzzzzzdddddabc')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('abcd', 'dddddddabc')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('dddddddabc', 'abcd')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('eabcd', 'dddddddabc')\n    False\n    >>> same_chars('abcd', 'dddddddabce')\n    False\n    >>> same_chars('eabcdzzzz', 'dddzzzzzz')\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    return sorted(s0) == sorted(s1)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import doctest\n    doctest.testmod()\n```\n\nThis function uses the `\nsorted` function to check if both strings contain all the same characters. If the unique, sorted characters of both strings are identical, then the strings have the same characters.",
